.TH PRCHUM 1 "2026-08-28" "prchum 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prchum \- review pull requests, git comparisons and patches
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prchum
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ target ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prchum
opens a review window for
.IR target .
With no argument inside a git repository it shows what
.BR "git diff" (1)
would print.
.PP
Comments anchor to a file, a side and a line range, with a short context
anchor and a hash of the line's content. A draft survives the branch
moving under it, and survives the request being updated.
.PP
prchum stores no credentials. Forges are reached through the command
line tools you have already authenticated:
.BR gh (1)
for GitHub,
.BR glab (1)
for GitLab, and a configurable command for Forgejo.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-staged ", " \-\-cached
Compare the index against HEAD, as
.B git diff \-\-staged
does.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH TARGETS
The argument is read the way git reads one.
.TP
.I (none)
The working tree against HEAD. Outside a repository, the home screen.
.TP
.I revision
That revision against HEAD, by merge base \(em
.IR revision ...HEAD .
.TP
.IR a .. b ", " a ... b
A range, spelled as git spells it.
.TP
.I path
A patch file, an exchange document, or a directory holding a git
repository.
.TP
.I number
That numbered request in the current repository's origin.
.TP
.IR owner / repo # number
A request in a named repository.
.TP
.I URL
A request URL from any supported forge.
.PP
A path that exists takes precedence. A file named
.B main
in front of you is the file you meant, not the branch of the same name.
A request is recognised by a
.BR # ,
a
.BR ! ,
a URL scheme, or by being all digits, so the branch
.B fix/thing
reads as a revision.
.SH GIT INTEGRATION
git runs any
.B git\-*
on the PATH as a subcommand, so
.B git prchum
works and takes the same arguments. It changes to the repository's top
level first, giving the same result from a subdirectory as from the
root.
.PP
To reach for it the way you reach for
.BR "git diff" (1):
.PP
.RS
.EX
git config \-\-global alias.d '!git prchum'
.EE
.RE
.PP
.B git d
then opens the working tree, and
.B git d main
compares against a branch.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/prchum/config.json
Configuration on Linux. On macOS,
.IR "~/Library/Application Support/Prchum/config.json" .
Unknown keys survive every save, and a file prchum cannot parse is never
overwritten.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/prchum/
Drafts, review history, and worktrees prchum created.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B prchum
exits non\-zero when the target cannot be read: no such file, no changes
in the comparison, or a forge that could not be reached.
.SH EXAMPLES
Review uncommitted work:
.PP
.RS
.EX
prchum
.EE
.RE
.PP
Review a branch against the trunk:
.PP
.RS
.EX
prchum main
.EE
.RE
.PP
Review a pull request:
.PP
.RS
.EX
prchum owner/repo#418
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git\-prchum (1),
.BR git\-diff (1),
.BR gh (1),
.BR glab (1)
.PP
Documentation: https://perrito666.github.io/prchum/
